WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:02.140
- What is this story
behind this song you're

00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:03.170
singing today "Throw Me A Party"?

00:00:03.170 --> 00:00:05.640
- Okay, so "Throw Me A Party" I wrote with

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:08.830
the amazing song writers
Liz Rose and Christian Bush

00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:10.010
from the band Sugarland.

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:13.140
And a few years ago, you know,

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:15.210
you kinda hear the words
that you never, ever

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:16.950
think you're gonna hear or
that you ever wanna hear,

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.500
which is you have cancer.

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:20.920
And I found out that I had breast cancer

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.330
and had a bilateral mastectomy,

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:25.977
and I'm a survivor sitting
here today talking to you.

00:00:25.977 --> 00:00:27.028
- That's so awesome.

00:00:27.028 --> 00:00:28.447
(audience clap and cheer)

00:00:28.447 --> 00:00:30.520
- It was so interesting
'cause when you're going

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:32.000
through something like that and you really

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.380
don't know what it's going to be like

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:34.500
and how it's gonna turn out,

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.360
and you don't know if you're
gonna be sitting here.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:37.260
- [Kelly] And you have kids.

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:39.514
- And you have kids, and I
wanted to have these very

00:00:39.514 --> 00:00:42.357
serious discussions with my
husband and I said to him,

00:00:42.357 --> 00:00:45.244
"look if something happens
and I should go before you

00:00:45.244 --> 00:00:46.978
"then I just want you to know

00:00:46.978 --> 00:00:48.657
"there's a couple of things I want.

00:00:48.657 --> 00:00:51.909
"One, I want you to be super
sad for a real long time."

00:00:51.909 --> 00:00:53.361
(audience laugh)

00:00:53.361 --> 00:00:55.510
- Like, I will hunt you if
you date someone next week.

00:00:55.510 --> 00:00:57.364
- Exactly, like I will hunt you.

00:00:57.364 --> 00:01:00.473
And then the second things
was that I wanted a party.

00:01:00.473 --> 00:01:02.530
I wanted to have a celebration

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:04.530
and I wanted to have a
lot of singing and dancing

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:06.003
and people telling stories,

00:01:06.003 --> 00:01:11.003
and to feel like that
was being celebrated.

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:14.020
And so the song came out of that.

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:17.660
I had the title and wrote
it with Liz and Christian.

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:18.730
- [Kelly] It's great.

00:01:18.730 --> 00:01:19.563
- Thank you.

00:01:19.563 --> 00:01:21.630
- Like I was telling you, I've never heard

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:23.062
a song that I will listen
to all the time like.

00:01:23.062 --> 00:01:26.860
And also perfect, there are,
it's a hard thing a funeral,

00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:27.810
and I've had to sing at funerals.

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:28.680
I don't know if you've
had to do that before?

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:30.070
It's the worst thing ever.
- No'

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:33.680
- Don't say yes, and it's
just the worst thing ever.

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:35.855
And it should be, sometimes I feel like

00:01:35.855 --> 00:01:38.830
we're this culture that
we just get so depressed

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:40.000
by it and it is a very depressing thing.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:42.370
But at the same time, like celebrate

00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:43.400
the life that was lived.

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:44.233
- Exactly.

00:01:44.233 --> 00:01:46.450
- And that's what I loved
about the whole lyric.

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:47.283
It was so perfect.

00:01:47.283 --> 00:01:48.330
- 'Cause there's gonna be time.

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:50.360
There's gonna be crying and
there's gonna be sadness.

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:51.193
- And that's okay.

00:01:51.193 --> 00:01:54.440
- And you never ever
forgot, you know, a person.

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:55.273
You never do.

00:01:55.273 --> 00:01:57.810
I think about my mom and
dad every single day.

00:01:57.810 --> 00:01:58.916
- [Kelly] And they're in you.

00:01:58.916 --> 00:01:59.749
- Exactly.

00:01:59.749 --> 00:02:00.582
- They're a part of you.

00:02:00.582 --> 00:02:02.440
My five-year-old is literally
learning about death

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:04.190
right now just 'cause
she was seeing something.

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:05.023
I'm like, "you're five."

00:02:05.023 --> 00:02:07.130
This is a hard conversation,
but I keep telling her,

00:02:07.130 --> 00:02:08.955
I'm like, "even if something
was ever to happen to mommy

00:02:08.955 --> 00:02:11.227
"I'm never really gone
because you are in me

00:02:11.227 --> 00:02:12.340
"and we're apart of each other."

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:13.173
- Yes.

00:02:13.173 --> 00:02:14.990
- And so I'm always present,
and it's like really hard,

00:02:14.990 --> 00:02:17.676
you find yourself kind of
talking yourself through death

00:02:17.676 --> 00:02:19.750
while you're trying to tell your child.

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:20.590
- That's exactly right.

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:22.316
You're trying to kind
of wrap your head around

00:02:22.316 --> 00:02:25.620
your own mortality and
that's the weirdest thing,

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:28.190
but I have to say that in someways,

00:02:28.190 --> 00:02:29.780
and I don't know if
there's survivors or people

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:31.730
who have had struggles in the audience

00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:34.910
but in someways cancer was a blessing,

00:02:34.910 --> 00:02:38.371
like it really taught
me to live every moment

00:02:38.371 --> 00:02:43.340
to the fullest and every
moment as if it was your last.

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:45.160
Like we don't know what tomorrow brings.

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:48.655
We have to be able to live
and go out today going,

00:02:48.655 --> 00:02:50.867
"wow, okay, I did it.

00:02:50.867 --> 00:02:52.437
"I did everything that I wanted to do.

00:02:52.437 --> 00:02:54.787
"I lived the life that
I wanted to live today."

